{"completion_status":"complete","final_message":"Moved post-integration worktree/branch removal outside the exec-lifecycle lock for register and schedule runs; integration and bookkeeping stay inside the lock, post-cleanup bookkeeping reacquires it. Added a per-worktree cleanup lock that makes re-runs, resumes, and `exec worktree remove` refuse while a cleanup is in progress. Added regression tests showing the lock is released before cleanup. Ticket results updated, including the CHANGELOG entry draft.","handoff":["Decision: post-review runs after the worktree removal (outside the first lock section, reacquiring the lock). When removal fails the item stays in review without post-review, so integration resume redoes cleanup and post-review without running post-review twice.","Decision: the post-review diff range (`outputCommit`) is fixed to HEAD right after the merge, so commits made by other items while cleanup runs do not widen it.","Decision: register cleanup takes a per-worktree lock (`exec/.locks/worktree-cleanup/<worktree>`) inside the exec-lifecycle lock. Same-item setup, resume, integration resume, and `exec worktree remove` refuse while it is live. A crashed cleanup leaves a stale lock that the next operation takes over; the next run or `exec worktree prune` removes the remains.","Decision: schedule (`runPreparedTask`) uses the same deferred-cleanup structure but has no per-worktree lock. Its lifecycle lock is the in-process `SerialAsyncLock`, and the task stays `doing` during cleanup, so the scheduler does not pick it again.","Decision: register removal failures now use the reason prefix `integrate cleanup failed` in the normal integration path too, distinguishing them from pre-merge `integrate failed`.","Remaining issue: `removeWorktree` uses `spawnSync`, so the cleanup still blocks the same process's event loop. Other processes (`specdojo git`, `--join` runs, register bookkeeping) no longer wait, but items running in parallel in the same process do not advance during cleanup. Making the removal asynchronous is a candidate for a separate register item.","CHANGELOG (Fixed): `exec run` の worktree 実行で、統合の後の worktree と exec branch の撤去を exec-lifecycle のロックの外で行うようにした。遅いファイルシステムで撤去に時間がかかっても、別の項目の記帳と `specdojo git` が待たされない。撤去の間は同じ項目の再実行・再開・`exec worktree remove` を拒否する。"],"validations":[{"command":"npm run validate:history-links","status":"passed","summary":"History-link validation passed including the updated ticket."},{"command":"npm run check:src-imports","status":"passed","summary":"src runtime imports are declared in dependencies or peerDependencies."},{"command":"npx prettier --write (changed .ts/.md files)","status":"passed","summary":"Changed TypeScript, test, and ticket files formatted with Prettier."},{"command":"npx markdownlint-cli2 docs/ja/projects/prj-0001/controls/project-register/pjr-nht7-worktree-cleanup-outside-lifecycle-lock.md","status":"passed","summary":"0 issues in the updated ticket."},{"command":"specdojo catalog validate","status":"not_applicable","reason":"Only a project-register ticket under docs/ja/projects changed; no catalog-managed deliverable was changed, and the catalog check is not part of this plan's required validations."}]}
